<protocol name="product_photography" type="domain" domain="visual">

## PURPOSE

Expert knowledge for commercial product photography.
This protocol contains what a $50K/shoot photographer KNOWS - composition, lighting, materials, quality standards.

Load this when you need visual expertise for product imagery.

---

## THE $50K DIFFERENCE

| Element | Amateur ($500) | Master ($50K) |
|---------|----------------|---------------|
| **Lighting** | Even, flat, "well-lit" | Reveals form, creates depth, tells story |
| **Composition** | Product centered | Product dominates with intentional negative space |
| **Material** | Shows the product | Glass sparkles, metal gleams, texture becomes tactile |
| **Background** | Clean white | Supports product without competing |
| **Edges** | Clean enough | Surgically perfect, ready for any composite |
| **Emotion** | "Here's the product" | "You need this in your life" |

**The Core Insight:** Amateurs light products so you can SEE them. Masters light products so you can FEEL them.

---

## COMPOSITION

### Product Dominance

| Task Type | Frame Coverage | Why |
|-----------|---------------|-----|
| Catalog hero | 70-85% | Product commands attention |
| Lifestyle | 40-60% | Context matters, product anchors |
| Detail/macro | 90%+ | Showcasing specific feature |
| Family shot | 60-80% total | Main hero + supporting variants |

### Negative Space Strategy

Negative space is intentional, not empty.

| Position | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| **Top** | Marketplace text overlay, title space |
| **Right** | Copy placement, social media captions |
| **Left** | Editorial layout flexibility |
| **Bottom** | Product anchoring, ground plane |

**Hero shot default:** Generous top (30-40% of frame), balanced sides.

### Camera Angle Psychology

| Angle | Effect | Use For |
|-------|--------|---------|
| **Eye level** | Equality, relatability | Lifestyle, approachable products |
| **Slight top (15-20 deg)** | Authority, overview | Catalog hero, product mastery |
| **Dramatic top (45 deg)** | Graphic, pattern-focused | Flat-lay, texture showcase |
| **Low angle** | Power, premium | Luxury, aspirational products |

**Catalog default:** Slight top (15-20 degrees) - shows product with authority.

### Rule of Thirds

- **Use it:** Lifestyle shots, editorial, multi-product compositions
- **Break it (center):** Single hero shots where symmetry creates impact
- **Power points:** Place key features at intersection points

---

## LIGHTING

### The Language of Light

Light reveals form. Shadow creates dimension. Together they tell the story.

| Light Quality | Effect | Use For |
|---------------|--------|---------|
| **Hard light** | Sharp shadows, texture emphasis | Texture showcase, dramatic mood |
| **Soft light** | Gradual transitions, flattering | Beauty, approachable products |
| **Diffused** | Even, no harsh shadows | Catalog standard, clean aesthetic |

### Three-Point Lighting (Studio Standard)

```
        [BACK/RIM]
            |
            |
         [PRODUCT]
        /         \
   [KEY]           [FILL]
   45deg           opposite
   main light      shadow fill
```

| Light | Purpose | Typical Ratio |
|-------|---------|---------------|
| **Key** | Main illumination, creates form | 100% (reference) |
| **Fill** | Opens shadows, reduces contrast | 30-50% of key |
| **Rim/Back** | Separation from background, edge definition | 50-100% of key |

### Lighting Ratios

| Ratio | Look | Use For |
|-------|------|---------|
| **1:1** | Flat, even | Documentation, not creative |
| **2:1** | Soft, commercial | E-commerce standard |
| **3:1** | Dramatic, editorial | Premium products, impact |
| **4:1+** | High contrast, moody | Luxury, artistic |

**Catalog default:** 2:1 to 3:1 - professional without being dramatic.

### Direction Psychology

| Direction | Effect | Use For |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| **Front** | Flat, informational | Technical documentation |
| **45 deg side** | Form-revealing, dimensional | Standard product photography |
| **90 deg side** | Dramatic texture | Texture showcase |
| **Back/rim** | Glow, separation | Glass, translucent materials |
| **Top** | Graphic, flat-lay | Pattern products, food |

---

## MATERIALS

### Glass (Clear, Colored, Frosted)

**Challenge:** Glass is invisible without light. Must reveal depth and edge.

| Technique | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| **Backlight** | Creates glow, reveals transparency depth |
| **Dark field** | Defines edges against light background |
| **Bright field** | Shows internal details, caustics |
| **Gradient reflections** | Shows form on curved surfaces |

**Excellence markers:**
- Internal caustics visible (light bending through)
- Edge refraction sharp and clean
- You can "see into" the glass, not just through it
- Speculars controlled but present (life, not flat)

### Metal (Polished, Brushed, Matte)

**Challenge:** Metal reflects everything. Must control reflections to show form.

| Surface | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Polished** | Large soft source for smooth gradients, tight specular control |
| **Brushed** | Directional light perpendicular to brush direction |
| **Matte** | Soft even light, avoid harsh speculars |

**Excellence markers:**
- Gradient reflections that follow form (not random hotspots)
- Controlled speculars that define edges
- Micro-texture visible (especially brushed)
- No burned highlights (detail preserved)

### PET / Plastic (Clear, Colored, Textured)

**Challenge:** Plastic looks cheap without care. Must show premium quality.

| Aspect | Technique |
|--------|-----------|
| **Surface sheen** | Side light reveals surface quality |
| **Labels/prints** | TACK SHARP - often the hero feature |
| **Translucency** | Backlight where appropriate |
| **Texture (honeycomb, etc.)** | Rake light at angle to reveal depth |

**Excellence markers:**
- Surface reads as quality, not cheap
- Any text/graphics are razor sharp
- Texture has dimensional feel (not flat)
- Colors accurate, vibrant but not oversaturated

### Fabric / Textile

**Challenge:** Fabric has micro-texture that defines quality. Must reveal weave.

| Technique | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| **Rake light** | Reveals weave texture |
| **Soft key** | Flattering drape shadows |
| **Low angle fill** | Opens fold shadows |

**Excellence markers:**
- Weave texture visible
- Drape shadows show dimensionality
- Fiber detail at edges
- Color accurate across folds (no crushed shadows)

### Ceramic / Porcelain

**Challenge:** Matte vs gloss surfaces need different treatment.

| Surface | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Matte** | Even soft lighting, avoid speculars |
| **Gloss** | Controlled speculars that define form |
| **Textured** | Rake light for texture, soft overall |

**Excellence markers:**
- Surface finish reads correctly (matte vs gloss)
- Even lighting without hotspots
- Texture preserved (not smoothed out)
- Clean edges, no color fringing

### Food & Beverage

**Challenge:** Food must look fresh, appetizing, ready to eat. The "freshness window" is critical.

| Element | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Texture** | Enhance crunch, moisture, steam where appropriate |
| **Color** | Vibrant but natural - never oversaturated |
| **Context** | Ingredients, preparation, serving suggestion |
| **Props** | Complementary items (utensils, napkins, ingredients) |

**Category-specific treatments:**

| Category | Key Techniques |
|----------|----------------|
| **Beverages** | Condensation droplets, pour shots, ice clarity, liquid color depth |
| **Baked goods** | Warm lighting, crumb detail, steam suggestion, golden tones |
| **Fresh produce** | Water droplets, natural imperfections OK, vibrant greens |
| **Packaged food** | Show contents AND packaging, serving suggestion |
| **Honey/syrups** | Drip shots, backlight for glow, viscosity visible |

**Excellence markers:**
- Would you want to eat/drink this RIGHT NOW?
- Freshness reads immediately
- Texture is tactile (you can almost taste it)
- Color is appetizing, not artificial
- Context feels natural, not staged

**The Appetite Test:** Does this image make you hungry/thirsty?

### Electronics / Tech Products

**Challenge:** Screens, LEDs, and reflective surfaces require special handling.

| Element | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Screens** | Show content or clean black, avoid reflections |
| **LEDs/lights** | Subtle glow, not overblown |
| **Buttons/ports** | Detail visible, not lost in shadow |
| **Cables** | Neat, intentional arrangement |

**Excellence markers:**
- Screen content readable or intentionally off
- No distracting reflections on glass/plastic
- Product feels premium and functional
- Technical details visible but not overwhelming

### Jewelry / Small Items

**Challenge:** Macro photography requirements, extreme detail visibility.

| Element | Technique |
|---------|-----------|
| **Scale** | Include scale reference OR extreme close-up |
| **Detail** | Tack sharp on key features (stones, engravings) |
| **Sparkle** | Controlled highlights that show brilliance |
| **Background** | Usually dark or neutral to emphasize item |

**Excellence markers:**
- Intricate details crystal clear
- Metal finish reads true (gold vs silver vs rose gold)
- Gems/stones show depth and brilliance
- Clasp/closure details visible if relevant

